{"title":"Michael Yin","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Michael Yin","subtitle":"&emsp;&emsp;Doctoral Student at Chicago Booth&emsp;|&emsp;Micro Theory, Market Design, & EconCS","format":{"html":{"page-layout":"full"}}},"headingText":"Education","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n![](files/michael_yin_headshot.jpeg){.profile-photo}\n\nI am a first year PhD candidate at the University of Chicago Booth School of Business. I am interested in matching with endogenous market selection and privacy constraints, as well as applications like school choice and tech platforms. More broadly, I am a microeconomic theorist focused on market design and the intersection of economics and computer science.\n\n\n- Master Analysis and Policy in Economics (Summa Cum Laude)<span class=\"right\">Paris School of Economics, 2025—26</span>\n- Master of Arts in Statistics (Concurrent Masters Program)<span class=\"right\">Harvard University, 2021—22</span>\n- Bachelor of Arts in Applied Mathematics (Summa Cum Laude)<span class=\"right\">Harvard University, 2018—22</span>\n\n## Experience\n\n- Data Scientist at Holocene Advisors<span class=\"right\">2023—25</span>\n- Data Science Analyst at Blackstone<span class=\"right\">2022—23</span>\n- Quantitative Research Intern at QuantCo<span class=\"right\">2020—21</span>\n- Labor and Poverty Intern at the Council of Economic Advisors<span class=\"right\">2019</span>\n\n## Teaching\n\n- Inference (Harvard Stat 111)<span class=\"right\">2021</span>\n- Econometrics (Harvard Ec 1126)<span class=\"right\">2020</span>\n- Micro Theory (Harvard Ec 1011a)<span class=\"right\">2019</span>\n\n## Contact\n\n- Email: michael.yin (at) chicagobooth.edu","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n![](files/michael_yin_headshot.jpeg){.profile-photo}\n\nI am a first year PhD candidate at the University of Chicago Booth School of Business. I am interested in matching with endogenous market selection and privacy constraints, as well as applications like school choice and tech platforms. Mor